From 1c148ab093c0aaa43cefecba2ca091c1283b81c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oscar Nordstrom <13300531+n0rpan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:50:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: add Q3_K 8x8 repack with dotprod gemv and i8mm gemm

Add block_q3_Kx8, a size-neutral lossless re-encoding of 8 block_q3_K
rows (signed 3-bit weights packed as X/Y/Z shift triples, 6-bit scales
as nibble + 2-bit planes), the repack function, generic gemv/gemm, NEON
dotprod gemv and NEON i8mm gemm (with a dotprod fallback), the template
specializations and arch-fallback aliases.

Q3_K tensors (2-D and 3-D MoE experts) are selected for CPU_REPACK on
NEON+dotprod when ne[1] % 8 == 0. GGML_CPU_REPACK_Q3K=0 disables the
selection at runtime (Q3_K weights then stay in the plain CPU buffer
and use ggml_vec_dot_q3_K_q8_K as before).

The kernels compute the same exact int32 super-block sums as
ggml_vec_dot_q3_K_q8_K and accumulate with the same fused multiply-add
order, so results are bitwise identical to the NEON vec_dot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
